Vermilion_NSFNCAR-UCAR-UCP_BrandGuide.pdf
.playwright-mcp/
# ⚠️ Playwright/MCP writes snapshots and screenshots to the CWD when a relative
# filename is passed, not into .playwright-mcp/ — so they land in the repo root.
# Smoking the XRAS cards means rendering UNSCRUBBED production PII, and two such
# files (a page snapshot and a full-page PNG) were caught one `git add` away
# from a public repo. Ignore them by shape rather than relying on the reviewer.
page-????-??-??T*.yml
*-pane.md
*-before.png
*-after.png
# ⚠️ It happened AGAIN on 2026-08-21 — `remediations-light.png` and
# `roles-modal-aligned.png` reached a commit, because the shape patterns above
# only guessed at the names a future session would choose. Matching names is
# whack-a-mole; the invariant is structural instead: real image assets live in
# `src/webapp/static/img/`, so a PNG at the REPO ROOT is a screenshot artifact.
# (`badge-light.png` predates this and is already tracked, so it is unaffected —
# gitignore does not untrack.)
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp
legacy_sam
data/

# Raw XRAS action payloads carry real names, emails and phone numbers. They are
# staged outside the working tree (~/xras_payloads_raw/) and reach the repo only
# after scripts/xras/scrub_payload.py. These patterns are the belt to that braces.
xras_payloads_raw/
*_payloads_raw/
